    },
    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 523,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Ribosomal protein S9 is a novel B23/NPM-binding protein required for normal cell proliferation.\nWe determined that S9 is a short-lived protein in the absence of ribosome biogenesis, and proteasomal inhibition significantly increased S9 protein level. Overexpression of B23 facilitated nucleolar storage of S9, whereas knockdown of B23 led to diminished levels of nucleolar S9. Our results suggest that B23 selectively stores, and protects ribosomal protein S9 in nucleoli and therefore could facilitate ribosome biogenesis."
     }
    ],
    "status": "ok"
   },
